+/* THE JOURNEY’S EDGE ON `/` (2026-10-08, the owner’s rule: the header’s edge is the page’s edge at every width).
+   The journey header and every page (`PageContainer`, `px-3 lg:px-6` = 16 / 32) keep one gutter: 16 below 1024 and
+   32 from 1024. The hero and the bands step to 24 at 768 instead, so on `/` their content sat 8px inside the header
+   from 768 and 8px outside it from 1024 (the visual pass’s tiles 017/018 and 047/048). The hero and every band on `/`
+   use these two containers, so this one rule lines the whole page up.
+   ⭐ SCOPED TO THE JOURNEY BY ITS SERVER-RENDERED MARK (`shell-mark.ts`): the span is in the HTML before any script
+   runs, so the first paint already has these values and nothing moves on hydration. Classic viewers are served what
+   they were (VODACOM-PLAN §0i, `qa:classic-shell-parity`): the classic home keeps its 24. A browser without `:has()`
+   keeps 24 too, which is the classic look and not a break. */
+@media (min-width: 768px) {
+  :root:has(#kp-journey-shell) .kp-hero__inner,
+  :root:has(#kp-journey-shell) .kp-band__inner { padding-inline: var(--sp-4); }
+}
+@media (min-width: 1024px) {
+  :root:has(#kp-journey-shell) .kp-hero__inner,
+  :root:has(#kp-journey-shell) .kp-band__inner { padding-inline: var(--sp-8); }
+}
 
